## 🕷️ 6. Onliner Scraping — Lessons Learned

### 6.1 Category Slugs
- The correct category slug for **kitchen hoods** on `catalog.onliner.by` is **`hoods`** (not `hood`, `kitchen_hood`, `cooker_hood`, `extractors`, etc.).
- Always verify an unknown slug by launching a Playwright browser, navigating to `https://catalog.onliner.by/` first to establish a session, then fetching `https://catalog.onliner.by/sdapi/catalog.api/search/{slug}?page=1` from inside `page.evaluate()`. A `200` response with `total > 0` confirms the slug.
- Known working slugs: `oven_cooker` (ovens), `hob_cooker` (cooktops), `hoods` (kitchen hoods), `dishwasher` (dishwashers).

### 6.2 Brand Filtering via the API Does Not Work
- The Onliner search API **does not support server-side brand filtering** via query parameters. All variants tested (`brand[]=bosch`, `brand[0]=bosch`, `manufacturer[0]=bosch`, `producer[0]=bosch`, `filter[brand][0]=bosch`) return the full unfiltered catalog (8,000+ results for `hoods`).
- **Correct approach**: Fetch all pages of the category search API (`?page=N`), then **filter client-side by `item.manufacturer?.key` or `item.manufacturer?.name`**. For a category like `hoods` with 8,000+ products, scanning 15 pages (450 products) is sufficient to capture all entries for major European brands.
- Script template: see `scan_brand_hoods.ts` in the project root.

### 6.3 Two-Phase Scraping Pattern for Targeted Brands
When you need full specs + reseller prices for a specific set of brands:
1. **Phase 1 — Discovery** (`scan_brand_hoods.ts`): Paginate the search API, filter client-side, collect `{ key, brand, name, priceMin }` for each matching product. Save to `scratch/hood_candidates.json`. This is fast (~1 min for 15 pages).
2. **Phase 2 — Detail scrape** (`scrape_hood_candidates.ts`): Read the JSON, call `scraper.scrapeSingle(key, categoryId, brand)` for each entry. This fetches full specs from the product detail page, all reseller offers from the positions API, and up to 10 reviews. Saves everything to the SQLite DB.
- Place both scripts at the **project root**, not in `scratch/`, to avoid `ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND` errors with relative `src/` imports.

### 6.4 Spec Field Names in the DB (Hood Category)
The `specs_json` column uses Russian-language keys as scraped from `.product-specs__table` on the product detail page. Key field names for hoods:

| Data point | DB key |
| :--- | :--- |
| Max extraction capacity | `Максимальная производительность отвода` |
| Min extraction capacity | `Минимальная производительность отвода` |
| Max noise level | `Максимальный уровень шума` |
| Min noise level | `Минимальный уровень шума` |
| Installation type | `Монтаж` |
| Duct diameter | `Диаметр воздуховода` |
| Color | `Цвет` |
| Width | `Ширина` |
| Control type | `Управление` |
| Number of motors | `Количество моторов` |
| Motor power | `Мощность мотора` |
| Perimetral suction | `Периметральное воздухопоглощение` |
| Wi-Fi remote | `Удаленное управление (Wi-Fi)` |
| IR remote | `Пульт ДУ` |
| Energy class | `Энергоэффективность` |
| Built-in value | `для встраивания` (value of `Монтаж`) |

- Some spec keys are **section headers** that duplicate their own name as value (e.g., `"Шум": "Шум"`). Skip these — the actual values are in sub-keys like `Максимальный уровень шума`.
- Not all products populate every field. Always use a multi-key fallback `get(...keys)` pattern when querying specs.

### 6.5 `scrapeSingle` Script Placement
- `scrapeSingle(key, categoryId, brand)` constructs the product URL as `https://catalog.onliner.by/{categoryId}/{brand.toLowerCase()}/{key}`. Ensure `brand` is passed as the display name (e.g., `"Bosch"`, `"Electrolux"`), not the slug, as the method calls `.toLowerCase()` internally.
- Each `scrapeSingle` call launches its own browser instance and closes it when done. For 20 products this takes ~8–10 minutes sequentially. This is intentional to avoid session/cookie conflicts.

### 6.6 Freshness & Force-Refresh
- The scraper's 7-day cache check uses the `category_id` column. Since brand-filtered scrapes still write to the same `hoods` category, a prior unfiltered `hoods` scrape will block subsequent runs unless `--force=true` is appended.
- Always add `--force=true` when running a targeted re-scrape of a category that has been previously scraped within 7 days.

